{
  "presses": ["L-ring-home", "L-middle-bottom", "R-pinky-top", "R-index-bottom-in"],
  "note": "From T1: chord {L-pinky-top (rotated aft), L-ring-home, L-middle-bottom, R-pinky-top} produced {A,M,R,V}. Rotation aft keys: L-index-home-in, L-index-top, L-pinky-top. T2: omit L-pinky-top; press {L-ring-home,L-middle-bottom,R-pinky-top,R-index-bottom-in}. Let S2 be returned set; compare with S1 to infer which 3 symbols are fixed for {L-ring-home,L-middle-bottom,R-pinky-top} (then remaining in S1 is L-pinky-top at T1). After T2, update which keys rotated; continue T3/T4 by omitting L-ring-home then L-middle-bottom (vary missing anchor) with new 4th keys."
}

{
  "presses": ["L-index-home-in", "L-ring-home", "R-index-bottom-in", "R-middle-home"],
  "note": "From T8 (no rotation on pressed keys): L-ring-home=A; R-middle-top=E; chord gave {A,E,P,U} so {L-index-home-in,R-index-home-in}={P,U}. Since in T6 those 3 keys {L-index-home-in,R-index-home-in,R-index-bottom-in}={C,P,U}, we get R-index-bottom-in=C. Plan: T9 press L-index-home-in+L-ring-home(A)+R-index-bottom-in(C)+R-middle-home(K). T10 press R-index-home-in +A+C+same K to resolve P vs U (if K not rotated)."
}

{
  "presses": ["L-ring-home", "R-middle-top", "R-index-bottom-in", "R-index-top-in"],
  "note": "T9: {L-index-home-in,L-ring-home,R-index-bottom-in,R-middle-home} -> {A,B,C,P}. Since T8 no-rot on pressed and {L-index-home-in,R-index-home-in}={P,U}, L-index-home-in at T9 press=P. Thus after T9-rot (L-index-home-in,R-index-bottom) swap => R-index-bottom-in=P. Remaining letters B,C on {R-index-bottom-in,R-middle-home} before rot => R-middle-home=B. Also R-index-home-in=U (not rotated in T9). From T6 group {L-index-home-in,R-index-home-in,R-index-bottom-in}={C,P,U} => at start T10 L-index-home-in=C."
}

{
  "presses": ["L-ring-home", "L-index-home-in", "R-index-home-in", "R-middle-top"],
  "locks": {
    "L-ring-home": "A",
    "R-index-bottom-in": "Z"
  },
  "note": "T11 (no rot): L-index-home-in=C, R-index-home-in=U, L-ring-home=A, R-index-bottom-in=Z. Next: press [L-ring-home,L-index-home-in,R-index-home-in,R-middle-top] => {A,C,U,x} so x=R-middle-top."
}

{
  "presses": ["L-ring-home", "R-index-home-in", "L-middle-bottom", "L-index-home-in"],
  "locks": {
    "L-ring-home": "A",
    "R-index-home-in": "U",
    "L-middle-bottom": "O"
  },
  "note": "From T14(no rotations): L-ring-home=A; {L-index-home-in,R-index-bottom-in}={C,Z}; R-index-home-in=U; L-middle-bottom=O. Next: press [L-index-home-in, L-ring-home, R-index-home-in, L-middle-bottom] to get letter on L-index-home-in (then R-index-bottom-in is other of {C,Z})."
}

{
  "presses": [
    "L-ring-home",
    "R-index-home-in",
    "L-index-bottom-in",
    "L-middle-bottom"
  ],
  "note": "T17: use anchors L-ring-home(A), R-index-home-in(U), L-middle-bottom(O) + test L-index-bottom-in. Expect symbols set {A,O,U,x}; if no rotation among these, x=letter on L-index-bottom-in, so L-ring-bottom gets remaining {N/R} from T16."
}

{
  "presses": ["L-index-home-in", "L-ring-home", "L-index-bottom-in", "R-index-home-in"],
  "locks": {
    "L-ring-home": "A",
    "L-index-bottom-in": "N",
    "L-index-home-in": "Z",
    "R-index-home-in": "U"
  },
  "note": "Solved (no rotation last): L-ring-home=A; L-index-bottom-in=N; R-index-home-in=U; thus L-index-home-in=Z."
}
